Texas Railroad Commission public records
----------------------------------------

The paths below are derived from public records of the Railroad Commission
of Texas (RRC): one night's Drilling Permit (W-1) imaged files, the Drilling
Permit Master daily file (daf420.dat), and the RRC record-layout manual
OGA049M. They remain under the RRC's terms. They are excluded from the MIT
License, and the MIT grant in LICENSE does not apply to them.

Source and date. The RRC files are listed in demo/corpus/manifest.json, one
entry per file with its URL and fetch date. All three were fetched on
2026-09-04: the W-1 imaged files (subscriptions_2026-09-03.zip) and the
Drilling Permit Master daily file from mft.rrc.texas.gov, and the OGA049M
manual from www.rrc.texas.gov.

The terms, quoted (web pages as read on 2026-10-22):

- RRC site policies (https://www.rrc.texas.gov/site-policies/): "RRC grants
  permission to copy and distribute the information on its website for
  noncommercial use, as long as the content remains unaltered and is not
  presented in a misleading way."
- That page points to the State Website Linking and Privacy Policy (Texas
  DIR, https://dir.texas.gov/resource-library-item/state-website-linking-and-privacy-policy),
  which says those who copy state agency information "must identify the
  source of the content, including the URL for the content or nearest entry
  point leading to the content if a URL is not available, and the date the
  content was copied."
- RRC Public Assistance, in a reply to the author on 2026-10-23: "raw
  factual public datasets and data available on the RRC website may be
  downloaded and reused in commercial data products." The reply says the
  "noncommercial use" wording in the site policies "is geared more towards
  branding, graphic design elements, and RRC-created expressive content,
  such as manuals and educational guides."

Not endorsed. This repository is not endorsed by the State of Texas, the
Railroad Commission of Texas, or any state agency.

Not the RRC's records. The paths below hold values extracted and re-keyed
from RRC files, not the files themselves. The fixtures in
demo/fixtures/responses/ are altered on purpose: each one says so in its
own "synthetic": true and "perturbations" fields. Do not read any of them as
an RRC record. The RRC reply above allows reuse of raw factual data like
these values, commercial use included. Before you reuse them, credit the
source as above. Also check the RRC's current terms and any notice that
comes with the source dataset or portal. The OGA049M manual is not in this
repository; only its field positions are used.

1. demo/corpus/manifest.json
   Source URLs, hashes, page counts, and class labels of the RRC files.
   Evidence, demo/corpus/manifest.json line 6:
     "url": "https://mft.rrc.texas.gov/link/f11363bb-8120-4e8c-bbc0-a253ec0a85d4",

2. demo/truth/ascii/*.json (9 files, one per permit)
   Fields from the RRC Drilling Permit Master daily file.
   Evidence, demo/build_corpus.py line 14:
     truth/ascii/<permit>.json       RRC ASCII master fields (SYSTEM-EXTRACTED, the different hand)
   Evidence, demo/truth/ascii/918133.json line 75:
     "basis": "RRC daf420.dat 2026-09-04, OGA049M positions"

3. demo/truth/w1/*.json (9 files, one per permit)
   W-1 form fields and word boxes from the RRC facsimile text layer.
   Evidence, demo/build_corpus.py line 15:
     truth/w1/<permit>.json          W-1 form fields from the facsimile text layer + word boxes (SYSTEM-EXTRACTED)
   Evidence, demo/truth/w1/918133.json line 312:
     "basis": "RRC W-1 facsimile text layer (pdftotext -layout / -bbox-layout); boxes normalized to page",

4. demo/truth/split/*.json (9 files, one per permit)
   Page ranges per class, with the RRC file names of each packet.
   Evidence, demo/build_corpus.py line 16:
     truth/split/<permit>.json       true page ranges per class (OBSERVED from packet assembly)

5. demo/truth/classify/*.json (26 files, one per RRC document)
   The class of each RRC document; each file name carries the RRC file name.
   Evidence, demo/build_corpus.py line 17:
     truth/classify/<permit>.json    true class per raw document (OBSERVED from RRC file naming)

6. demo/fixtures/responses/<permit>.json (9 files: 907829, 917176, 917669,
   918133, 918151, 918203, 918233, 918289, 918387)
   Synthetic parser responses generated from the truth files above, so they
   carry RRC values and RRC file names. The demo/fixtures/responses/synth/
   folder is not included here; it is synthetic.
   Evidence, demo/make_fixtures.py line 4:
     Every fixture is derived from truth plus labeled perturbations. The perturbation list is written into each
   Evidence, demo/fixtures/responses/918133.json line 9:
     "file": "918133_W1_AsApprovedW1-9-3-2026_LTR.pdf",

Not shipped
-----------

The RRC permit PDFs (demo/corpus/raw/), the assembled packets
(demo/corpus/packets/), and the permit master daily file are not in this
repository. demo/build_corpus.py rebuilds them from local copies; its source
URLs, on mft.rrc.texas.gov and www.rrc.texas.gov, are at
demo/build_corpus.py lines 31-33.

